course: dictionary
lesson: 11750
title: One word, many meanings: balancing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find out which one the author means by reading the words around it. The word balancing is a good example. «Mia stood on one foot, balancing on the beam.» Here balancing means keeping steady so you do not fall.
explain: «The scales were balancing, with three red bricks on each side.» Now balancing means the two sides weigh the same. The clues are the scales and the equal bricks. Always ask: which meaning fits here? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: «Dad was balancing the books, making sure the money coming in matched the money going out.» Here balancing means making money match. The same word can change its meaning, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Balancing means keeping something steady so it does not fall, like balancing on a beam.
fact: Balancing means making two sides weigh or be worth the same, like a balance scale with equal weights.
fact: Balancing money means making sure what comes in and goes out match.
fact: «A balanced diet» means eating a good mix of foods, and «a balancing act» means something hard to keep steady.
fact: Balance is the root word: balance, balances, balanced and balancing all come from it.
exercise: «Lia was balancing a tray of cups as she walked.» What does balancing mean here? | Running very fast | Counting the money in the tin | Making two things weigh the same | *Keeping steady so nothing falls
exercise: «The teacher added a weight to the lighter side, balancing the scale.» What does balancing mean here? | Writing a long story | *Making both sides weigh the same | Dropping things on the floor | Walking across a bridge
exercise: «Sam was balancing the club's money, so the cash in matched the cash out.» What does balancing mean here? | Losing coins down a drain | Painting the club sign | *Making money coming in and going out match | Kicking a ball hard
test: «Ben kept his arms out wide, balancing on the low wall.» What does balancing mean here? | Counting coins into a jar | Making the wall taller | Shouting for help | *Keeping steady so he does not fall
test: «Both pans of the scale held five apples, so they were balancing.» What does balancing mean here? | Walking in a line | *Weighing the same on each side | Cooking supper | Falling over slowly
exam: «Balancing on one foot is harder than it looks, said the coach.» Which meaning fits best? | *Keeping steady without falling | Making a shopping list | Making two teams the same size | Adding up the points at the end
